  "explanation": "\n\nAfter deducting the trader’s 0.10 % cost per trade, the rule generated a total return of roughly +86 % while being invested only about 36 % of the days. This falls short of the fair S&P 500 benchmark that earned +108.6 % on the same active days, and it is well below the simple buy‑and‑hold return of +239.2 % for GC=F over the full period. The strategy’s Sharpe ratio of 0.57 and a maximum drawdown of –15.2 % indicate modest risk‑adjusted performance and only moderate downside risk. Because no robustness check was presented, there is no clear evidence that the edge is genuine rather than a product of luck.  \nVerdict: **Weak**.",
  "code": "import yfinance as yf\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nimport json\n\ndef download_close(ticker: str, start: str) -> pd.Series:\n    \"\"\"Download adjusted close series with retries.\"\"\"\n    for attempt in range(3):\n        try:\n            df = yf.download(ticker, start=start, auto_adjust=True, progress=False)\n            if df is not None and not df.empty:\n                close = df[\"Close\"].squeeze()\n                if isinstance(close, pd.Series):\n                    return close\n                if isinstance(close, pd.DataFrame) and close.shape[1] == 1:\n                    return close.iloc[:, 0]\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        time.sleep(3)\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Failed to download {ticker} after 3 attempts\")\n\n# 1. Download data\nstart_date = \"2015-01-01\"\ngc = download_close(\"GC=F\", start_date)\ntnx = download_close(\"^TNX\", start_date)\ndxy = download_close(\"DX-Y.NYB\", start_date)\nspy = download_close(\"SPY\", start_date)\n\n# 2. Align all calendars to GC (traded asset)\nmaster_idx = gc.index\ntnx = tnx.reindex(master_idx, method=\"ffill\")\ndxy = dxy.reindex(master_idx, method=\"ffill\")\nspy = spy.reindex(master_idx, method=\"ffill\")\n\n# 3. Compute signals on day T close\n# TNX: absolute change <= -5 bps (-0.0005 in decimal yield terms)\n# DXY: percent change <= -0.3%\nsignal = (tnx.diff() <= -0.0005) & (dxy.pct_change() <= -0.003)\nsignal = signal.fillna(False)\n\n# 4. Build holding period (1 on entry day T through day before exit)\nholding = pd.Series(0.0, index=master_idx, dtype=float)\ngc_vals = gc.values\nsignal_dates = signal[signal].index\n\nfor entry_dt in signal_dates:\n    entry_iloc = master_idx.get_loc(entry_dt)\n    if holding.iloc[entry_iloc] == 1.0:\n        continue  # already in a position\n    entry_price = gc_vals[entry_iloc]\n    target_price = entry_price * 1.015\n    exit_iloc = entry_iloc\n    # Check up to 4 trading days forward (T+1 .. T+4)\n    for i in range(1, 5):\n        check_iloc = entry_iloc + i\n        if check_iloc >= len(gc_vals):\n            break\n        if gc_vals[check_iloc] >= target_price:\n            exit_iloc = check_iloc\n            break\n    else:\n        # Max 4 trading days held (exit at T+4 close)\n        exit_iloc = min(entry_iloc + 4, len(gc_vals) - 1)\n    # Holding = 1 from entry_iloc to exit_iloc-1 inclusive\n    holding.iloc[entry_iloc:exit_iloc] = 1.0\n\n# 5. Position, returns, costs\nposition = holding.shift(1).fillna(0.0)\ngc_ret = gc.pct_change().fillna(0.0)\nstrat_ret = position * gc_ret\n\n# Transaction cost 0.1% per entry (round trip) on first day of position\nentries = (position.diff() == 1.0)\nstrat_ret[entries] -= 0.001\n\n# 6. Equity curves\nstrat_eq = (1.0 + strat_ret).cumprod()\nspy_ret = spy.pct_change().fillna(0.0)\nspy_eq = (1.0 + spy_ret).cumprod()\n\n# 7. Metrics\ntotal_return = float(strat_eq.iloc[-1] - 1.0)\nbuy_and_hold_return = float(gc.iloc[-1] / gc.iloc[0] - 1.0)\n\npos_mask = position == 1.0\nspy_same_days_return = float((1.0 + spy_ret[pos_mask]).prod() - 1.0)\nn_pos_days = int(position.sum())\nspy_random_days_return = float((1.0 + spy_ret.mean()) ** n_pos_days - 1.0)\n\ndaily_ret = strat_ret\nmean_ret = daily_ret.mean()\nstd_ret = daily_ret.std()\nsharpe = float(mean_ret / std_ret * np.sqrt(252)) if std_ret > 0 else 0.0\n\ndd = strat_eq / strat_eq.cummax() - 1.0\nmax_drawdown = float(dd.min())\n\nn_trades = int(entries.sum())\ntime_in_market = float(position.sum() / len(position))\n\n# 8. Save equity.csv\neq_df = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"date\": strat_eq.index,\n    \"strategy\": strat_eq.values,\n    \"spy\": spy_eq.values\n})\neq_df.to_csv(\"equity.csv\", index=False)\n\n# 9. Output RESULT\nresult = {\n    \"traded_ticker\": \"GC=F\",\n    \"total_return\": total_return,\n    \"buy_and_hold_return\": buy_and_hold_return,\n    \"spy_same_days_return\": spy_same_days_return,\n    \"spy_random_days_return\": spy_random_days_return,\n    \"time_in_market\": time_in_market,\n    \"sharpe\": sharpe,\n    \"max_drawdown\": max_drawdown,\n    \"n_trades\": n_trades\n}\nprint(\"RESULT \" + json.dumps(result))\n",
