    "The signal for TNX incorrectly uses percent change instead of absolute change in basis points; a 5 bp drop in ^TNX (quoted in percent) corresponds to an absolute change of –0.0005, not a –0.0005 (‑0.05 %) percent change. This mis‑specifies the entry condition and generates wrong signals. Fix: compute the absolute difference with `tnx.diff()` and use `(tnx.diff() <= -0.0005) & (dxy.pct_change() <= -0.003)` for the signal."
